# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: A snapshot-guided blocker declaration converges when two creatures
#   can block but Forge AI wants only Centaur Courser assigned.
# Forcing: Valley Dasher must attack. Centaur Courser kills it without dying,
#   while zero-power Yoked Ox cannot satisfy the destruction goal.
# AI behavior: Valley Dasher is required to attack. Forge AI prefers the free
#   Courser kill over the nonlethal Ox block.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN = Centaur Courser was assigned, the partial declaration was submitted,
#     and Valley Dasher died in combat.
#   LOSE = no useful block was submitted and Valley Dasher survived combat.
#   TIMEOUT = blocker selection toggled without converging on Submit.
# Card roles:
#   Valley Dasher — forced attacker and destruction target.
#   Centaur Courser — intended blocker that wins combat without dying.
#   Yoked Ox — legal but nonlethal second blocker that keeps the
#     committed declaration partial.
# Protocol path: DeclareBlockersReq -> snapshot consultation -> iterative
#   DeclareBlockersResp -> SubmitBlockersReq.
# Harness assertion: exactly one block response, then one submit response, with
#   no unblock response; the block must name Centaur Courser.

[metadata]
Name:Partial Blocker Convergence
Goal:Destroy Specified Creatures
Targets:Creature.OppCtrl
Turns:1
Difficulty:Easy
Description:Choose one useful blocker from two legal blockers, then submit the partial declaration.

[state]
ActivePlayer=AI
ActivePhase=Main1
HumanLife=20
AILife=20

humanbattlefield=Centaur Courser;Yoked Ox
humanlibrary=Forest
aibattlefield=Valley Dasher
ailibrary=Plains
